WEBVTT

00:00:00.029 --> 00:00:01.779
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:06.250
In this lesson, we will make location information useful and current.

00:00:06.699 --> 00:00:11.060
A map can mislead when old positions remain visible or useful sites

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:12.619
and reference layers are missing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:16.190
We will explain the features, the setup decisions, and a

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:18.129
practical way to check the result.

00:00:18.719 --> 00:00:22.709
A department adds its stations and hospitals as points of interest and

00:00:22.709 --> 00:00:27.729
lets personnel locations expire after 60 minutes so old positions disappear.

00:00:28.229 --> 00:00:32.240
A current map shows where responders and apparatus are and puts important

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.250
locations in front of dispatchers.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:38.679
The examples in this series use a fictional department and are teaching

00:00:38.679 --> 00:00:40.980
scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:42.160
Mapping.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.429
The live map of personnel, units and calls.

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:49.109
Set how long locations stay on the map in the mapping settings.

00:00:49.469 --> 00:00:51.720
Availability also depends on Mapping.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:54.140
Check access in the target department.

00:00:54.989 --> 00:00:56.089
Points of Interest.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:01:00.310
Points of interest such as stations, hospitals and hydrants.

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:03.029
Add the locations dispatchers need to see.

00:01:03.519 --> 00:01:05.769
Availability also depends on Mapping.

00:01:06.239 --> 00:01:08.239
Check access in the target department.

00:01:08.869 --> 00:01:10.460
Weather zones and alerts.

00:01:10.909 --> 00:01:13.410
Weather alert zones and alert notifications.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.629
Draw the zones you cover and choose who is alerted.

00:01:17.329 --> 00:01:18.220
Map Layers.

00:01:18.579 --> 00:01:20.960
Add your own shapes and overlays to the map.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.829
Confirm members allow location sharing in the Responder app, and decide how

00:01:25.829 --> 00:01:27.760
long a position should stay on the map.

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:30.430
Availability also depends on Mapping.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.760
Check access in the target department.

00:01:33.449 --> 00:01:34.270
Live Routing.

00:01:34.679 --> 00:01:37.400
Directions and routes for responding resources.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:42.060
Confirm members allow location sharing in the Responder app, and decide how

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.020
long a position should stay on the map.

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:46.670
Availability also depends on Mapping.

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:49.149
Check access in the target department.

00:01:49.819 --> 00:01:51.130
Custom map layers.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:55.029
Upload your own map images, such as a campus or venue map.

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:59.739
Confirm members allow location sharing in the Responder app, and decide how

00:01:59.739 --> 00:02:01.630
long a position should stay on the map.

00:02:02.109 --> 00:02:04.550
Availability also depends on Mapping.

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:06.960
Check access in the target department.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:08.590
Indoor maps.

00:02:09.019 --> 00:02:11.149
Floor plans and zones for buildings.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:15.870
Confirm members allow location sharing in the Responder app, and decide how

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:17.759
long a position should stay on the map.

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:20.530
Availability also depends on Mapping.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.150
Check access in the target department.

00:02:23.769 --> 00:02:24.369
Routes.

00:02:24.779 --> 00:02:28.280
Planned routes, such as patrols, and who is assigned to them.

00:02:28.769 --> 00:02:33.080
Confirm members allow location sharing in the Responder app, and decide how

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:34.969
long a position should stay on the map.

00:02:35.429 --> 00:02:37.809
Availability also depends on Mapping.

00:02:38.269 --> 00:02:40.430
Check access in the target department.

00:02:41.039 --> 00:02:43.730
For the training scenario, work in this order.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:44.799
Step 1.

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:48.240
Review personnel and unit location-age settings.

00:02:48.619 --> 00:02:49.400
Step 2.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:52.540
Add stations and hospitals as points of interest.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:53.660
Step 3.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:58.660
Add a relevant map layer, planned route, or weather zone and review its audience.

00:02:59.309 --> 00:03:00.819
Now verify the result.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:05.829
Check marker age and source, POI placement, reference-layer alignment,

00:03:06.009 --> 00:03:08.249
and the intended weather-alert coverage.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:13.299
A common problem to watch for: Location sharing requires client permission.

00:03:13.839 --> 00:03:17.819
Uploaded floor plans are reference material; verify currency and

00:03:17.819 --> 00:03:19.739
alignment before relying on them.

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:22.019
Your practice task is simple.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:26.709
Follow a sample unit and compare a recent position with a stale position.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:30.509
Record missing POIs and outdated reference layers.

00:03:30.929 --> 00:03:34.729
Record the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

